        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0702" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg616"/>

                <head>No. 263.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_CEDL1"
                            type="from">De Long</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation, Yokohama, Japan</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            21, 1873</date>. (Received July 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 433.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    just received a note from Senor Aurilio Garcia y Garcia, the Peruvian envoy,
                    which reads as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation del Peru,
                                Yedo</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 20, 1873.</p>
                        <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Friend</hi>: After a very long
                            discussion with the minister for foreign affairs, Mr. Woogem, which I
                            asked for in view of his answer to my dispatch on the Maria <pb
                                facs="0703" n="617" xml:id="pg617"/> Luz case, we agreed yesterday
                            and have signed a protocol referring that case to the arbitration of the
                            chief of a friendly state. The difference between Peru and Japan has
                            thus ended.</p>
                        <p>The only thing to be done now is to select the arbitrator and submit the
                            case to him.</p>
                        <p>Convinced that this news will be gratifying to you,</p>
                        <p>I am, yours very sincerely,</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">A. G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">y</hi> GARCIA.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>His Excellency <persName corresp="#p_CEDL1"><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. E. De
                            Long</hi></persName>, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_CEDL1">C. E. DE LONG</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
